@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "maxTurns: 5,",
+  "cause": "The `triage` agent, which is the entry point the customer's chat talks to, is defined without a `store`, so Genkit treats it as client-managed and rejects any attempt to resume it by `sessionId`.",
+  "evidence": "Before the fix, `triage.chat({ sessionId })` threw `FAILED_PRECONDITION: Cannot use 'sessionId' with agent 'triage': this agent has no store configured` (the check in @genkit-ai/ai agent.ts assertInitMatchesStateManagement). Adding `store` (the same FileSessionStore that `refundAgent` already uses) made the resume succeed, and a two-turn run of 'My order is A-1001.' followed by a resumed 'What is its status?' returned the A-1001 status."
+}
